   "hand": "Drag across the specimen to lift the skin flaps away from the midline.",
   "text": "Lift the skin from the midline and turn the flaps laterally, keeping the knife against the underside of the skin so the fat stays behind. You are now in the superficial fascia: find the cephalic vein in the deltopectoral groove, the basilic vein on the inner arm, the supraclavicular nerves crossing the clavicle, the external jugular vein and platysma in the neck.",
