   "info": {
    "lies": "Ventral ramus of C5. It leaves between the C4 and C5 vertebrae and passes between scalenus anterior and scalenus medius.",
    "clinical": "C5–C6 injury (a fall on the shoulder, or traction on the head during a difficult birth) causes Erb’s palsy: the arm hangs adducted and medially rotated with the forearm pronated, the ‘waiter’s tip’ position."
   },
   "layer": "nerves"
  },
