   "site": "Roots C8 and T1",
   "cause": "The arm is pulled upward, for example clutching at a branch during a fall, or a breech delivery with the arm above the head. A cervical rib or an apical lung tumour can compress the lower trunk more slowly.",
   "sees": "Claw hand: the knuckles are hyperextended and the finger joints flexed, with wasting of the small muscles of the hand.",
   "moves": "Fine movements of the fingers, spreading and closing the fingers, and grip.",
   "reflex": "The finger flexor jerk (C8) is reduced.",
   "signs": "Horner syndrome (drooping eyelid, small pupil, dry face on that side) if T1 is torn close to the spinal cord."
